  "description": "Two-gate KEM encapsulation (SIGE spec 5.2-5.5) from fixed randomness. Seed derivation (src/core/vectors.ts): seededBytes(label, length) concatenates SHA-256 blocks sha256(seedDomain + '/' + label + u32be(counter)) for counter = 0, 1, 2, ..., truncated to length bytes; seededScalar(label, order) reduces seededBytes(label + '#' + attempt, 48) mod order, retrying attempt = 0..7 on a zero result. xA = seededScalar(xASeed, Fr.ORDER), xB = seededScalar(xBSeed, Fr.ORDER), full-range BLS12-381 scalars; pkA/pkB = G2.BASE * x, compressed hex. idWarrant/idLog are gateIdentity() outputs (see gate-identity.json, same networkId/accountId/enrollmentId/epoch), hashed to G1 under domain-separation tags DST.warrant = \"SIGE-DEMO-WARRANT-V1\" and DST.log = \"SIGE-DEMO-LOG-V1\". transcriptHash = seededBytes(transcriptHashSeed, 32), context = seededBytes(contextSeed, 32); plaintext is a literal utf8 string, not seeded. U/K come from encapsulate(), whose randomness is r = reduce(dhash(\"fo-randomness\", plaintext, transcriptHash, context)) mod Fr.ORDER, rehashing and retrying on a zero result, where dhash(domain, ...parts) = SHA256(\"SIGE-DEMO/v1\" || u32be(len(domain)) || domain || u32be(len(part)) + part for each part). zA/zB from deriveContribution() on each gate; combineContributions(zA,zB,...) must equal K. Independently cross-checked: U via a from-scratch dhash (node:crypto sha256) FO-randomness rederivation, K via node:crypto hkdfSync over the captured zA||zB.",
